    "title": "Phrase of the week",
    "text": "Knock on wood: A superstitious phrase or physical action used to avoid bad luck or “tempting fate” after making a hopeful statement, boast or mentioning good fortune. Ancient Celtic and Germanic tribes believed good and evil spirits lived inside trees. Tapping a tree trunk supposedly summoned the benevolent spirits for protection or thanked them for good fortune.",
